      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Titanium dioxide is a whitening ingredient used in foods, cosmetics, and other products. It is considered safe by the FDA, but high intake could be harmful. It is also known as titanium (IV) oxide or titania. When used as a pigment, it is called titanium white, Pigment White 6 (PW6), or CI 77891. It is a white solid that is insoluble in water. It is a naturally occurring mineral existing in a number of crystalline forms, the most important of which are rutile and anatase.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "二氧化钛是一种用于食品、化妆品和其他产品的美白成分。美国食品和药物管理局认为它是安全的，但大量摄入可能有害。它也被称为钛（IV）氧化物或二氧化钛。用作颜料时，它被称为钛白、颜料白 6 (PW6)或 CI 77891。它是一种不溶于水的白色固体。它是一种天然矿物，有多种结晶形式，其中最重要的是金红石型和锐钛矿型。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
